    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0628" n="532" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg532"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hitchcock to Mr.
                            Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-06-07"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 84.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your No. 69, of May 23, relating to the designation of the first secretary of
                    this embassy as conseiller. I note that in the opinion of the Department this
                    could only be done by statutory authority; but for reasons given in my No. 54,
                    of April 30, I trust the Department may see fit to secure such legislative
                    enactment as will cover this point.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ethan A. Hitchcock.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
